The first assertion checks if the return value of the `IndexOf` method is non-negative, which means that the element has been successfully added to the list. The second assertion verifies that the last index of the element in the new array list is less than or equal to the old array list's count, which implies that the element has been added at the correct position within the list.

Please note that Debug.Assert is a debugging tool and is not intended to be used in production code. It throws an AssertFailedException if the condition inside the parentheses is false, indicating a bug in the program. This allows developers to catch and fix issues early in the development process.--------------------```cs
Debug.Assert(New_Ret >= 0 && New_arrListCount <= Old_arrListCount);
